            <div xml:id="d240-a2">

                <pb facs="0352" n="246" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg246"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure A.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Captain Schley to the intendente of
                    Valparaiso</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">U.
                                S. S. Baltimore</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Valparaiso</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform your excellency
                    that my men who were wounded in the disturbance of October 16 last are now able
                    to appear as cited by the judge of the criminal court, and will be accompanied
                    by an officer as interpreter, who will authenticate such testimony as may be
                    given.</p>
                <p>I would request, at the same time, that his honor will oblige me by appointing
                    the earliest practicable day for this hearing.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. S. Schley</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Captain Commanding</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
